          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="edge5" edge="1" parent="1" source="resref" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;startArrow=ERone;endArrow=ERzeroToMany;startFill=0;endFill=0;strokeColor=#526d82;strokeWidth=2.5;fontSize=14;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;jumpStyle=arc;jumpSize=12;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;startArrow=ERzeroToOne;" target="moves" value="optional reservation">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="edge6" edge="1" parent="1" source="invref" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;startArrow=ERone;endArrow=ERzeroToMany;startFill=0;endFill=0;strokeColor=#526d82;strokeWidth=2.5;fontSize=14;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;jumpStyle=arc;jumpSize=12;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;" target="moves" value="stock movement history">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note0" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=15;fillColor=#fef3c7;strokeColor=#d49a20;fontSize=17;" value="Additional FKs (not repeated as crossing lines): orders.cancelled_by, recipes.updated_by, order_status_history.changed_by and stock_movements.performed_by -&gt; users.id; stock_movements.order_id -&gt; orders.id; stock_movements.ingredient_id -&gt; inventory.ingredient_id. Cancellation users are nullable until cancellation." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="1710" y="1400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note1" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=15;fillColor=#fef3c7;strokeColor=#d49a20;fontSize=17;" value="Audit entity_id is a polymorphic logical reference qualified by entity_type, not a SQL FK to multiple tables. ADJUSTMENT movements may omit order_id and reservation_id. For order movements, enforce that reservation_id, order_id and ingredient_id identify the same reservation. password_hash stores a secure password hash, never plaintext." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="1710" y="1540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="fhg05j3Fa-NikHzjmxu3" name="3 - Constraints and Rules">
    <mxGraphModel dx="543" dy="559" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="827" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=30;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#123047;" value="PantryChef | Database Constraints and Transaction Rules" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="65" width="1710" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note0" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=15;fillColor=#fef3c7;strokeColor=#d49a20;fontSize=17;" value="01 | Keys and referential integrity&#10;recipes: PK(menu_item_id, version).&#10;recipe_lines: PK(menu_item_id, recipe_version, ingredient_id); composite FK to recipes.&#10;order_items: composite FK(menu_item_id, recipe_version) to recipes; UK(order_id, id).&#10;reservations: composite FK(order_id, order_item_id) to order_items; UK(order_item_id, ingredient_id).&#10;All other *_id foreign keys target the named parent PK; stock_movements.ingredient_id targets inventory.ingredient_id, the 1:1 stock row of ingredients.id. Retain historical references with ON DELETE RESTRICT." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="330" width="820" y="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note1" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=15;fillColor=#fef3c7;strokeColor=#d49a20;fontSize=17;" value="02 | Row-level CHECK constraints&#10;Stock: on_hand &gt;= reserved AND reserved &gt;= 0.&#10;Recipe version &gt;= 1; recipe/reservation quantity &gt; 0.&#10;Order item quantity BETWEEN 1 AND 50.&#10;Prices, order total and low_stock_threshold &gt;= 0. ingredients.name is UNIQUE.&#10;Unit IN (g, ml, piece); no conversion in the MVP.&#10;resolved_at IS NULL for ACTIVE; required for CONSUMED or RELEASED.&#10;Validate finite numeric input and field lengths before writes." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="330" width="820" x="890" y="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note2" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=15;fillColor=#fef3c7;strokeColor=#d49a20;fontSize=17;" value="03 | Valid states and cancellation data&#10;orders.status IN (PENDING, PREPARING, READY, CANCELLED).&#10;reservations.status IN (ACTIVE, CONSUMED, RELEASED).&#10;users.role IN (WAITER, CHEF, MANAGER).&#10;Cancellation requires cancelled_by, cancelled_at, previous_status and late_cancellation; pending cancellation may omit a reason.&#10;Late cancellation additionally requires a 3-500 character reason. Server checks MANAGER or WAITER + ORDER_LATE_CANCEL.&#10;Legal transitions and user permissions are enforced by the service." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="340" width="820" y="480" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note3" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=15;fillColor=#fef3c7;strokeColor=#d49a20;fontSize=17;" value="04 | Recipe versions and snapshots&#10;Partial UNIQUE(menu_item_id) WHERE is_current = true ensures at most one current version. Service ensures one current recipe per orderable menu item.&#10;Each change inserts a new immutable recipe version; new versions may reference only active ingredients (service check, 422 INGREDIENT_INACTIVE).&#10;Order items preserve menu_item_name_snapshot, unit_price and recipe_version; reservations preserve ingredient name/unit and quantity.&#10;Recipe and order minimum line counts are enforced within their transaction; a normal FK cannot enforce at least one child." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="340" width="820" x="890" y="480" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note4" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=15;fillColor=#fef3c7;strokeColor=#d49a20;fontSize=17;" value="05 | Atomic stock invariants&#10;Create order: lock inventory rows in stable ingredient order, check all available quantities, then save PENDING order + ACTIVE reservations and increase reserved.&#10;Start preparation: lock order and stock rows; change ACTIVE to CONSUMED; decrease on_hand and reserved equally, once.&#10;Pending cancel: ACTIVE to RELEASED; decrease reserved only. Late cancel: no stock restore. READY: no stock movement.&#10;reserved = SUM(ACTIVE reservations) is cross-table: maintain in the same transaction, not a row CHECK." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="340" width="820" y="860" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note5" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=15;fillColor=#fef3c7;strokeColor=#d49a20;fontSize=17;" value="06 | Idempotency and stock movement consistency&#10;UNIQUE scope is the composite PK(user_id, operation_scope, idempotency_key). Include order ID in status operation_scope.&#10;Atomically claim key and fingerprint; same body replays saved status/body/headers; a different body is rejected.&#10;Claim and successful response commit with business effects; rollback must not leave a permanently locked IN_PROGRESS claim.&#10;Partial UNIQUE(reservation_id) WHERE type = CONSUME prevents a second consumption movement. Service also serializes reservation state changes." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="340" width="820" x="890" y="860" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note6" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=15;fillColor=#fef3c7;strokeColor=#d49a20;fontSize=17;" value="07 | Movement and audit rules&#10;stock_movements.type IN (RESERVE, RELEASE, CONSUME, ADJUSTMENT). RESERVE quantity &gt; 0; RELEASE and CONSUME &lt; 0; ADJUSTMENT != 0. After-values satisfy on_hand_after &gt;= reserved_after &gt;= 0.&#10;Order movements require order_id and reservation_id; enforce FK(reservation_id, order_id, ingredient_id) to a matching UNIQUE(id, order_id, ingredient_id) on reservations.&#10;Adjustment reason: INITIAL_STOCK, PURCHASE_RECEIVED, PHYSICAL_COUNT_CORRECTION, WASTE, LATE_CANCELLATION_CORRECTION or OTHER.&#10;Audit actions: ORDER_CANCELLED, ORDER_LATE_CANCELLED, STOCK_ADJUSTED, RECIPE_UPDATED, USER_PERMISSIONS_CHANGED, INGREDIENT_DEACTIVATED, INGREDIENT_REACTIVATED. Entity types: ORDER, INGREDIENT, MENU_ITEM, USER." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="370" width="820" y="1240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note7" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=15;fillColor=#fef3c7;strokeColor=#d49a20;fontSize=17;" value="08 | Indexes, retention and scope&#10;Suggested indexes: orders(status, created_at); order_items(order_id); reservations(ingredient_id) WHERE status = ACTIVE; recipe_lines(ingredient_id); stock_movements(ingredient_id, created_at); order_status_history(order_id, changed_at); audit_logs(occurred_at).&#10;Also index other referencing FK columns where query/deletion patterns need it; PostgreSQL does not create all FK indexes automatically.&#10;Users are deactivated; menu items archived. Ingredients are deactivated (active = false), never hard-deleted; existing PENDING reservations still complete. Preserve recipe, reservation and audit history.&#10;This is a proposed schema, not a deployed database. No SQL migration or runtime test has been executed." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="370" width="820" x="890" y="1240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
